<title>FRANCE: Usinor interim net profit 833 mln Ffr. [corrected 06:42 gmt]</title>
<headline>Usinor interim net profit 833 mln Ffr. [corrected 06:42 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects net profit figure in headline and table to 833 mln Ffr from 800 mln Ffr)</p>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>			 (Figures in millions of francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			  833     vs	   2,360</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional	    1,205     vs	   3,808</p>
<p>    Cash flow				 2,919     vs	   4,260</p>
<p>    Turnover				 37,392     vs	  41,625</p>
<p>    Industrial investments (billions)   1.8     vs	  1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Usinor Sacilor the fall in turnover of around 10 percent from a year ago was due mainly to lower volumes, as the effect from higher prices had been limited. Net debt at the first half stage totalled 8,351 million francs, compared to 11,044 million at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>The ratio of net debt to equity improved to 0.29 from 0.38 at the end of 1995, consistent with the group's objective of strengthening its financial structure.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
